als in hushed tones that Tom has a mistress in New York. Daisy later confides in Nick her cynical hope that her daughter will be a 'beautiful little fool,' a statement Nick perceives as a hollow performance. As Nick returns home to West Egg, he stops on his lawn and observes Gatsby standing alone, arms outstretched toward a distant green light across the bay, before Gatsby vanishes into the night.</div>\n                ","numLines":500,"startLine":300,"totalLines":19466}}}
